BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 693.77 Tm (Section 3: Where Practitioners Disagree & Alternative Playbooks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 671.55 Tm (The sharpest split on the street is the knowledge bar. Amanda Lockaby tells prospective relators that the key) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 656.32 Tm (is demonstrating intentional fraud and that mistakes or negligence are not enough [OfdepsSYjp4 @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 641.10 Tm (00:01:29]. Mark Kleiman runs the opposite playbook. In his reading the statute says intent to defraud is not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 625.87 Tm (required, reckless disregard and deliberate indifference are enough, and in practice the bar sits near gross) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 610.65 Tm (negligence [yN7NRjwYKFs @ 00:31:35]. Maryanne Hamilton and Darth Newman side with Kleiman. They) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 595.42 Tm (frame the Act as no negligence statute that also carries no intent-to-defraud requirement, and their classic) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 580.20 Tm (proof is a biller who objects and is told "just do it that way. That's how we get paid" [HocnawRgrAA @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 564.97 Tm (00:19:55]. Andrew Hillman reads the knowingly definition the same way, folding in deliberate ignorance and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 549.75 Tm (reckless disregard, and states that no proof of specific intent to defraud is required [AcMsQCQm5QI @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 534.52 Tm (00:01:54]. The split drives intake screening. A Lockaby-style intake rejects sloppy-billing files that a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 519.30 Tm (Kleiman-style intake pushes forward when the paper trail shows someone was warned and kept billing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 504.07 Tm (anyway. Teams on the reckless-disregard threshold work a wider pipeline of files built on warnings that were) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 488.85 Tm (ignored. Teams anchored on intentional fraud run a narrower docket and pass on cases built only on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 473.62 Tm (carelessness.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 458.40 Tm (Money splits are the second fault line. Against The Fraud pitches a flat 15 to 30 percent and treats) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 443.17 Tm (first-to-file as winner-take-all. Later relators get nothing, it is a literal race to the DOJ, and absolute urgency) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 427.95 Tm (is required [QmB-gKtr0tc @ 00:08:17]. Kleiman describes a softer market. Shares run 15 to 25 percent on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 412.72 Tm (intervened cases and 25 to 30 percent on declined ones, mostly by negotiation. The first relator commonly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 397.50 Tm (keeps 85 to 90 percent, so a later filer still carves out a slice [yN7NRjwYKFs @ 01:24:16]. Brown, LLC splits) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 382.27 Tm (the difference. With full overlap the later filer is out and the first filer has no duty to share, though parties) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 367.05 Tm (sometimes negotiate an arrangement anyway. Non-overlapping claims, such as back braces in one) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 351.82 Tm (complaint and injections in another, can both proceed [3ugChIElhkM @ 00:11:57]. Cory Reiss quotes the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 336.60 Tm (intervened band as "15 to 20 25%", depending on how helpful the information was, rising to as much as 30) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 321.37 Tm (percent once a declined case unseals [7-9Z8vNWVFc @ 00:02:28]. The operator has to pick a lane. One) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 306.15 Tm (option is to sprint and file early to lock priority under the race model. The other is to file a tighter,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 290.92 Tm (non-overlapping theory and negotiate a split if a rival relator surfaces later.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 275.70 Tm (Timelines diverge just as hard. Hamilton and Newman have seen seals last 12 months at the fastest and 10) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 260.47 Tm (years at the longest. They call 2 to 3 years the good side of average and say 5 years is not unexpected) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 245.25 Tm ([HocnawRgrAA @ 00:36:19]. Brown, LLC pegs the average at about two and a half years and reports that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 230.02 Tm (the government literally always wants more time to investigate [3ugChIElhkM @ 00:07:08]. Michael) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 214.80 Tm (Granston puts DOJ's intervention decision at about 11 months across all cases. Relator counsel on the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 199.57 Tm (same panel concede that relators who are not ready to litigate after a declination quietly welcome extensions) Tj ET
