BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 628.77 Tm (Title: What the filing attorneys do that self-filers skip) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 613.55 Tm (Body: These are the packaging and sequencing moves practitioners use to keep a claim from going into the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 598.32 Tm (circular file and to protect the award percentage later.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 583.10 Tm (Items: Hand over the killer email on day one; Zerbe sees stalled claims from clients who held evidence back) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 567.87 Tm (waiting for the IRS to call, and the IRS really only looks at a filing once [Kohn Kohn & Colapinto -) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 552.65 Tm (O45E7FrG_mM @ 00:09:24].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 537.42 Tm (If the information came through your role as an attorney or accountant, resolve that before filing or the claim) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 522.20 Tm (can sit in a taint process for three to five years [Brown, LLC - A Premier Whistleblower Law Firm -) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 506.97 Tm (tQIkb01vCTw @ 00:05:48].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 491.75 Tm (Describe supporting documents you do not hold but know exist, and tell the IRS exactly where to find them) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 476.52 Tm ([Teach Me! Personal Finance - WA3dtUQT9f8 @ 00:02:46].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 461.30 Tm (Plead that the target owes tax; Zerbe says showing fraud is a nice bonus, but all you need to show is that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 446.07 Tm (the person owes tax [Kohn Kohn & Colapinto - O45E7FrG_mM @ 00:17:40].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 423.85 Tm (3. Where Practitioners Disagree & Alternative Playbooks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 401.62 Tm (The sharpest split is whether to file Form 211 solo or behind counsel. Emily Stibil of Phillips and Cohen says) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 386.40 Tm (flatly that you don't need a lawyer to file a tip, positioning an attorney as a way to navigate the process and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 371.17 Tm (craft the tip so it heightens the likelihood of success [fQss6bE5tKc @ 00:00:34]. Jason T. Brown pushes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 355.95 Tm (much harder: you can fill out the form yourself, but Brown strongly discourages it, predicting a self-filed claim) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 340.72 Tm (will probably hurt the case and go into the circular file, while conceding that certain people have recovered) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 325.50 Tm (without an attorney [RuNrDW46nKY @ 00:12:28]. Alina of Oberhide PC sells counsel as a credibility signal,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 310.27 Tm (arguing the IRS has reason to believe law-firm submissions are genuine because the firm has already vetted) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 295.05 Tm (eligibility and substantiation and walks away from cases that fail either test [sNHauc7rutQ @ 00:08:46].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 279.82 Tm (Brown's intake desk shows what the solo route costs: many matters arrive after someone already submitted) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 264.60 Tm (their own Form 211 and wants it salvaged, the firm reviews whether it can even clean up the mess people) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 249.37 Tm (generally make on their own, and it declines on the spot when it can't [tQIkb01vCTw @ 00:06:18]. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 234.15 Tm (working read from the counsel camp is blunt: a botched first filing is treated as close to unrecoverable,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 218.92 Tm (because you only get one first bite at the apple.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 203.70 Tm (Case-size doctrine splits into two camps. Former IRS agent Mike Sullivan preaches whales only: the IRS) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 188.47 Tm (wants a big splash that can make the newspapers and please the commissioner, not a couple of bait fish on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 173.25 Tm (top of the water, and a small or undocumented claim is not worth anyone's time [41ejxu80Qtg @ 00:03:10].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 158.02 Tm (Bryan Skarlatos answers from twenty years of whistleblower practice that bigger is not better, reporting) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 142.80 Tm (many billion-dollar claims filed in a career and none of them paid, because a massive claim drags the IRS) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 127.57 Tm (into a very complex process [ruRW_hNSDYk @ 00:12:43]. Skarlatos expects hundred-million-plus cases to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 112.35 Tm (hit headwinds from complexity and well funded taxpayer defenses, and puts the sweet spot at 10 to 50) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 97.12 Tm (million dollars, or a tighter 10 to 25 million, while warning that a five or six million claim may not justify a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 81.90 Tm (ten-year wait for a 20 to 30 percent award once professional fees are counted [ruRW_hNSDYk @ 00:16:01].) Tj ET
